---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ToolPageShell from '../components/astro/ToolPageShell.astro';
import Faq from '../components/astro/Faq.astro';
import UnlockTool from '../components/tools/UnlockTool';
import { webAppJsonLd, faqJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';

const faq = [
  { q: 'Will this crack or guess a password for me?', a: 'No. This is not a password cracker. It requires the correct password to unlock the file — if you don’t know the password, this tool can’t help you get in.' },
  { q: 'Why would I unlock a PDF I already have the password for?', a: 'Mostly convenience — so you stop retyping a password every time you open your own bank statement, insurance form, or scanned document on a device where re-entering it is annoying.' },
  { q: 'Is it legal to unlock a PDF like this?', a: 'Yes, when it’s your own document and you’re using the password you legitimately know. This tool simply removes the password requirement from a file you already have full access to.' },
  { q: 'Is my PDF uploaded anywhere?', a: 'No. Decryption runs entirely inside your browser; the file and password never leave your device.' },
];
const description = 'Remove a password from a PDF you own — free, offline, in your browser. Requires the correct password; nothing is uploaded anywhere.';
---
<Base title="Unlock PDF — remove a known password, free | localdobe" {description} canonicalPath="/unlock-pdf"
  jsonLd={[webAppJsonLd('Unlock PDF', '/unlock-pdf', description), faqJsonLd(faq)]}>
  <ToolPageShell h1="Unlock a PDF" sub="Remove the password from a PDF you own — locally, using the password you know.">
    <UnlockTool client:load slot="tool" />
    <h2>How to unlock a PDF</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Drop your password-protected PDF into the box above (or click to browse).</li>
      <li>Enter the file’s current password.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Unlock PDF</strong> and download the unprotected file.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>This requires the correct password</h2>
    <p>Let’s be plain about this: localdobe’s unlock tool is not a password cracker. It removes an existing password from a PDF, but only if you supply the correct one. If you’ve genuinely lost the password to a file, this tool — and honestly, any legitimate tool — can’t get you back in.</p>
    <h2>Why people unlock their own PDFs</h2>
    <p>The most common reason isn’t secrecy, it’s annoyance: a bank statement, insurance form, or scanned document that demands a password every single time you open it. If it’s your document and you know the password, stripping that prompt is entirely legal — you’re just removing a restriction on a file you already have full access to. Unlocking runs locally, so the password and the file never leave your device.</p>
    <p>Want the details? Read <a href="/blog/remove-pdf-password/">how to remove a password from a PDF</a>.</p>
    <Faq items={faq} />
  </ToolPageShell>
</Base>
